KZ3 4001: one online switch, a host-name map and an egress allowlist for the network layer (libs/network/net_policy.c).
ps3_net_online() reads KZ3_ONLINE once (upstream form: PS3_NET_ONLINE) and every path that can open a real socket asks
it: ppu_sysprx (host sockets registered only when online), cellNetCtl (state), np_psnr (--psnr forces it on). Strict
mode (off unless a port enables it): gethostbyname resolves only mapped names (others HOST_NOT_FOUND, never the host
resolver), connect/sendto reach only allowlisted ip:port/protocol, port 53 always refused, each refused destination
logged once; denied name suffixes (telemetry) refused in any mode. Guest host names are length-bounded (256) before
use. Upstream tests that compile sysNet.c/np_psnr.c directly include net_policy.c. Test: tools/net/test_net.sh.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

